{"name":"Katsura","hex":"#c9e3cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Katsura","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A unisex given name from Japanese.","A surname from Japanese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Katsura"}],"entries":[{"title":"Katsura Imperial Villa","blocks":[{"text":"The Katsura Imperial Villa or Katsura Detached Palace  is an Imperial residence with associated gardens and outbuildings in the western suburbs of Kyoto, Japan. Located on the western bank of the Katsura River in Katsura, Nishikyō-ku, the Villa is 8km distant from the main Kyoto Imperial Palace. The villa and gardens are nationally recognized as an Important Cultural Property of Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Katsura_Rikyu_%283264799678%29.jpg/330px-Katsura_Rikyu_%283264799678%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katsura_Imperial_Villa","wikidata":"Q1736808"},{"title":"Cercidiphyllum","blocks":[{"text":"Cercidiphyllum is a genus containing two species of plants, both commonly called katsura. They are the sole members of the monotypic family Cercidiphyllaceae. The genus is native to Japan and China and unrelated to Cercis (redbuds)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/Cercidiphyllum_japonicum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cercidiphyllum","wikidata":"Q858028"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Katsura_Rikyu_%283264778634%29.jpg/500px-Katsura_Rikyu_%283264778634%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Katsura_Rikyu_%283264778634%29.jpg/1280px-Katsura_Rikyu_%283264778634%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https